**How to implement.** The absorbing ground truth and its measurement design move into `BerremanTestSupport` whole, beside their transparent twin (001 §Q AT-2 'The ground truth and designs (… `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`: constants, `buildAbsorbing`, the cuts, `a1` / `a2` / `a3`, `perturbedStart`, `searchBox`) move into a shared test-support project'; the S10.2 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples (test → product / test support) … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one `AbsorbingBiaxialSample` module exists. (1) `git mv Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`, and its namespace becomes `BerremanTestSupport`. Every declaration moves with its body unchanged, as S10.1 leaves it: the six ε″ components, `absorbing`, `absorbingScalingAround`, `plate`, `waveLength`, `opticAxisCut`, `otherOpticAxisCut`, `configuration`, `a1`, `a2`, `a3`, `fullConfigurations`, `perturbedStart` and `searchBox`. The retained `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.buildAbsorbing` MUST move with the module and MUST call `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.opticalProperties`, whose tensor kernel was extracted in step 334, `configuration` has passed `float<deg>` angles to `MuellerFitting.configurationOf` since step 335, and `SearchBox` has been `MuellerFitting`'s since step 337. The file keeps `open BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample` (step 345). No `open` of a `BerremanTests` module remains in it: `open BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness` is deleted, because after S10.1 nothing in the file reads the harness and `BerremanTestSupport` references no test project. In the module doc, the first paragraph gains one sentence citing spec 0050 S10.2 (001 §Q AT-2): the sample and its design live in `BerremanTestSupport`, so one compiled copy serves `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`. Every other doc line keeps its text. (2) `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` gains `<Compile Include="AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs" />` after `BiaxialSample.fs`. No reference and no comment is added. (3) `BerremanTests.fsproj` deletes `<Compile Include="AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs" />`, so its compile list holds no ground-truth file. (4) In `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs`, `open BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialSample` becomes `open BerremanTestSupport.AbsorbingBiaxialSample`, keeping its trailing comment. Nothing else in them changes. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): every expression is unchanged, and `fullConfigurations` holds the same 44 configurations in the same order. No test is added or removed. `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` (about 177 s) reads every moved declaration that `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` (946 s, not selected) reads, and it reaches the rest through `configuration` and `fullConfigurations`. The moved test-support module MUST still declare buildAbsorbing; every direct test caller MUST use the new namespace, and the old BerremanTests source MUST be deleted. Product code MUST use the parameter-record member and MUST NOT reference BerremanTestSupport. This preserves 001 §Q's named builder destination without copying physics.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` MUST declare the module `BerremanTestSupport.AbsorbingBiaxialSample` with every declaration and number unchanged and no `open` of a `BerremanTests` module. `Berreman/BerremanTests/` MUST neither hold nor compile `BiaxialSample.fs` or `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`, and both absorbing suites MUST open `BerremanTestSupport.AbsorbingBiaxialSample`. unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s34 invariants MUST pass. BerremanTestSupport.AbsorbingBiaxialSample.buildAbsorbing MUST exist and call the shared product kernel; the former BerremanTests source MUST be absent.
